# Z.AI Rules

Z.AI (GLM) is an OpenAI-compatible provider at the **GLM Coding Plan** base URL `https://api.z.ai/api/coding/paas/v4`.
Models: GLM series with thinking support.

## Model table

| Cursor alias     | Real model | Description                                          |
| ---------------- | ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |
| `gpt-4.1-turbo`  | `glm-5.3`  | Planning model; always thinks; reasoning_effort + prompt caching |
| `gpt-4.1`        | `glm-4.7`  | Budget execution; thinking on/off only               |
| (internal)       | `glm-4.6v` | **Vision worker** only — describes images for ALL providers. Not user-selectable; not in `/v1/models`. Runs on the coding-plan endpoint. |

`glm-4.6v` has **no Cursor alias** (level 1–2: label "Vision worker"; level 3:
model `glm-4.6v`). It is invoked by `vision.Describer` in the gateway; vision
usage bills under `zai::glm-4.6v`.

## API key

- Key field: `zaiKeyEncrypted` in `config.AppSettings`
- Set via: `discursive set --zai-key <key>` or `--zai-key` flag on `init`
- Retrieved via: `settings.GetZaiKey(dataRoot)` in gateway/server.go
- Z.AI is optional — the gateway works without it

